  "integration_notes": [
    "Stage A uses the five exact Rust 1.96 CI-formatted postimages already published at 1b86d19810c9d422a8f8ea3b76a0a2e8c9956585; do not apply it again. B starts from that commit. C preserves the entire formatted SourceWitness implementation byte-for-byte and adds exactly six immutable snapshot fixture constants.",
    "Stage D1 intentionally does not advertise episodic import capability or add AgentdState/config ingress fields. It handles the new exhaustive request variant with the existing unavailable error and tests the real UDS refusal.",
    "Stage D2 installs actual source/writer ingress and includes retained task/counter/unresolved fence before enabling control; D3 adds only the real App Server concurrency regression.",
    "Run just fmt and preserve/apply its exact diff before just test. Actual line counts must be measured after formatting; no line-limit pass is asserted.",
    "ProductionCognitiveMutationError adds TransactionSettlementUnknown; indexed exhaustive caller in memory-extension tools is included in B. Complete checkout rg is still needed to exclude unindexed newer exhaustive callers.",
    "Snapshots, original authority and source observations in tests are explicit fixtures. Real source custody/provider successor benefit are still separately unverified.",
    "V1 permanently retires an imported (source_id,key) slot. Even an explicitly written valid newer Python version is refused. This is narrower than MEM6 Python revoke-then-write semantics; it needs a separately authorized namespace or a future qualified native reconstruction path. Rejection does not prove full rebuild semantics.",
    "Original writer clones/capabilities share one Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<()>> for episodic imports. A queued import rechecks the existing native authority/gate after acquiring this lock and before BEGIN.",
    "Existing CognitiveCommitGate::transition_attempt changes no active commit permission when created. After BEGIN its guard is moved to a later binding than the Transaction: panic fences before transaction Drop queues rollback, then the shared import lock releases. Successful commit/rollback is explicitly awaited before acknowledge.",
    "Commit/rollback uncertainty may already have released SQLite's physical lock before it is observed. The retained import mutex nevertheless remains held until the native gate fence is installed, so a subsequent episodic import cannot BEGIN past that fence. Other ordinary native-owner writes before uncertainty is observed remain subject to the pre-existing native transaction contract; no stronger global serialization is claimed.",
    "The existing begin helper can fail after acquiring BEGIN IMMEDIATE. A guard held across begin fences before the shared episodic import mutex releases; the error is conservatively unresolved and does not establish that a memory mutation occurred.",
    "refresh_generation propagates the retained unresolved flag through existing mark_fenced. A dropped reply future is not required to observe JoinError for Health to become ready=false/fenced=true or ordinary CognitiveContext to refuse.",
    "ImportSource forwards the original typed source admission unchanged and checks the shared unresolved flag before and after each source read; it can only refuse, never confer source authority.",
    "Recovery anchor observation after fence uses the existing cognitive_store_recovery.rs observation transaction with explicit rollback. It is distinct from ordinary ready-gated CognitiveContext and no bypass interface is added.",
    "A preimages/postimages are already reviewed CI formatting. B/C/D sources are not yet formatted or natively validated; refresh downstream preimages only from reviewed formatter postimages, never by silently overwriting divergent source.",
    "Replay avoids another canonical memory revision/receipt mutation; protected owner Dirty coordination may still occur. It does not promise zero physical owner/checkpoint work."
  ],
